// A REFERENCE COPY. The real `go.work` is gitignored (.gitignore:8), because it
// wires up whatever modules happen to be checked out on one machine — and a
// machine path in a committed file breaks the build for everyone else.
//
// Copy this to `go.work` if you do not have one. Nothing requires it: the API
// module builds on its own, and CI sets GOWORK=off on purpose (ADR 0007), so a
// green CI run proves which toolnexus version the code ran against.
//
// IF GO SAYS THIS:
//
//	go: cannot load module ../../spikes listed in go.work file:
//	    open ../../spikes/go.mod: no such file or directory
//
// then your `go.work` names a module that is no longer in the tree — `spikes/`
// is the usual one, since it comes and goes. Delete that `use` line. No commit
// can fix it for you, because the file is not in the repository.

go 1.26.3

use ./apps/api

// Add this ONLY while spikes/ is present in your checkout. It verifies
// UNRELEASED toolnexus behaviour, so it builds against a local checkout while
// apps/api stays on the published version (ADR 0007) — do not add a `replace`
// for apps/api here, or a green run stops proving which code it ran against.
//
// use ./spikes
//
// And to point spikes/ at a local toolnexus working tree:
// replace github.com/muthuishere/toolnexus/golang => ../nexus-workspace/toolnexus/golang
